"zigzag":{"w":"zigzag","firstLevel":"初中","cn":"adj. “之”字形的；v. 弯弯曲曲行进；n. “之”字形；蜿蜒曲折","senses":[{"pos":"adj","cn":["“之”字形的"]},{"pos":"v","cn":["弯弯曲曲行进"]},{"pos":"n","cn":["“之”字形","蜿蜒曲折"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈzigzæg/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈzɪɡzæɡ/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=zigzag&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"But some, and this is interesting, move straight west while some <B>zigzag</B> or even move in large circles.","cn":"但是有趣的是，其中有一些会朝西直线移动，而另外的则会曲折前行，或者甚至绕着大圈子移动。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"He talks about a ship's voyage and this is one of the most famous bits of the essay—how the best voyage is made up of <B>zigzag</B> lines.","cn":"他讲到了关于船航行的例子，这是文中最著名的部分之一——最成功的航行是如何由曲折的航线组成的。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"A <B>zigzag</B> metal roof, also incorporated into the Oppenheimer Park design, now acts as a unifying design element throughout the district.","cn":"一个之字形的金属屋顶也被纳入奥本海默公园的设计中，现在成为整个地区统一的设计元素。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Mr Netanyahu will have to <B>zigzag</B> ever harder to keep his turbulent team together.","cn":"","src":"ECONOMIST","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · ECONOMIST"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[],"syn":[]},"tag":["ky","toefl","gre"],"collins":0,"oxford":0,"frq":17582,"img":"https://ydlunacommon.nosdn.127.net/c32f9104e4fbccca2971526c960802a1.png?","syl":{"n":2,"s":0,"l":["zig","zag"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex","fam_gap"]},
