"accustomed":{"w":"accustomed","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"adj. 习惯的；通常的；独有的；v. 使习惯于（accustom的过去分词）","senses":[{"pos":"adj","cn":["习惯的","通常的","独有的"]},{"pos":"v","cn":["使习惯于（accustom的过去分词）"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/əˈkʌstəmd/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/əˈkʌstəmd/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=accustomed&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"\"We're <B>accustomed</B> to having one thing in our pocket to do all these things,\" he added, \"and the average consumer isn't gonna be able to afford another device that's hundreds and hundreds of dollars.\"","cn":"","src":"2013·福建·阅读B","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2013年高考英语（福建）· 阅读B","year":2013,"region":"福建","section":"阅读B"},{"en":"They're <B>accustomed</B> to the rigours of army life.","cn":"他们已习惯了军旅生活的艰辛。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"Mary Jo is still <B>accustomed</B> to travelling everywhere in style.","cn":"玛丽·乔仍然习惯于很有气派地到处旅行。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"She was a person <B>accustomed</B> to having eight hours' sleep a night.","cn":"她是那种习惯每晚睡八个小时的人。","src":"牛津","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《牛津词典》（有道词典接口）"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"accustom","ph":"/əˈkʌstəm/","cn":"v. 使习惯"}],"syn":["customary"]},"tag":["gk","cet4","cet6","ky","toefl"],"collins":1,"oxford":0,"frq":8524,"img":"","syl":{"n":3,"s":1,"l":["ac","cu","stomed"]},"flags":["few_exam_ex","no_img"]},
