"compensate":{"w":"compensate","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"v. 补偿，赔偿；抵消","senses":[{"pos":"v","cn":["补偿","赔偿","抵消"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈkɒmpenseit/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈkɑːmpenseɪt/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=compensate&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Nothing can <B>compensate</B> for the loss of a loved one.","cn":"失去心爱的人是无法补偿的。","src":"牛津","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《牛津词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"The damages are designed to <B>compensate</B> victims for their direct losses.","cn":"该赔偿金是用来补偿受害人的直接损失的。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"A surge in domestic sales helped <B>compensate</B> for a fall-off in export sales.","cn":"国内销售的增长帮助补偿了出口销售的减少。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"Greenwald hopes to <B>compensate</B> in part by cutting the cost of getting tickets into passengers hands.","cn":"","src":"FORBES","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · FORBES"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"compensation","ph":"/.kɒmpenˈseiʃən/","cn":"n. 弥补，补偿"},{"w":"compensable","ph":"/kəmˈpensəbl/","cn":"adj. 可补偿的，应予以补偿的"}],"syn":["correct"]},"tag":["gk","cet6","ky","toefl","ielts","gre"],"collins":2,"oxford":0,"frq":5037,"img":"https://ydlunacommon-cdn.nosdn.127.net/92878c300687694f7f35c2a3c485c4d0.jpg?","syl":{"n":3,"s":0,"l":["com","pen","sate"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex"]},
