"dioxide":{"w":"dioxide","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"n. 二氧化物","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["二氧化物"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/daiˈɒksaid/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/daɪˈɑːksaɪd/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=dioxide&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"They are the base of the food chain, using photosynthesis to produce sugar from carbon <B>dioxide</B> and water.","cn":"","src":"2012·四川·阅读E","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2012年高考英语（四川）· 阅读E","year":2012,"region":"四川","section":"阅读E"},{"en":"Warming changes key characteristics of the ocean and can affect phytoplankton growth, since they need not only sunlight and carbon <B>dioxide</B> to grow, but also nutrients.","cn":"","src":"2019·北京（机考 无听力）·阅读D","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2019年高考英语（北京（机考 无听力））· 阅读D","year":2019,"region":"北京（机考 无听力）","section":"阅读D"},{"en":"Increased carbon <B>dioxide</B> (CO2) in the air from burning coal and oil can have an effect on how plants produce oxygen, while higher temperatures and changeable rainfall patterns can change their patterns of growth.","cn":"","src":"2012·四川·阅读E","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2012年高考英语（四川）· 阅读E","year":2012,"region":"四川","section":"阅读E"},{"en":"Humans take in oxygen and breathe out carbon <B>dioxide</B>.","cn":"人吸入氧气，呼出二氧化碳。","src":"牛津","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《牛津词典》（有道词典接口）"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[],"syn":[]},"tag":["gk","cet6","toefl","ielts"],"collins":0,"oxford":0,"frq":5712,"img":"","syl":{"n":3,"s":1,"l":["di","ox","ide"]},"flags":["no_img","fam_gap"]},
