"snatch":{"w":"snatch","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"n. 抢夺；抓举；小量；v. 夺得；抽空做；及时救助","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["抢夺","抓举","小量"]},{"pos":"v","cn":["夺得","抽空做","及时救助"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/snætʃ/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/snætʃ/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=snatch&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Hey, you kids! Don't all <B>snatch</B>!","cn":"嗨，孩子们！别抢啊！","src":"牛津","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《牛津词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"He is puzzled, rather than vengeful when other children <B>snatch</B> things from him or push him around.","cn":"当其他孩子从他手里抢东西或把他推来推去时，他感到困惑，而不是报复。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Their aggression is, although cute in a way, that at most they will try to <B>snatch</B> a sandwich from you at a picnic.","cn":"他们的攻击性，虽然在某种程度上很可爱，但他们最多只会在野餐时试图从你手中抢走一块三明治。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"And in stoppage time, Gerrard lashed in an angled shot to <B>snatch</B> the points.","cn":"","src":"BBC","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · BBC"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"snatcher","ph":"/ˈsnætʃər/","cn":"n. 抢夺者，抢夺贼，抢包贼；绑架者，绑匪"}],"syn":["bit"]},"tag":["gk","cet6","ky","ielts","gre"],"collins":2,"oxford":0,"frq":6071,"img":"https://ydlunacommon.nosdn.127.net/09ad4ac2a7704f6e62ed690e849afff4.png?","syl":{"n":1,"s":0,"l":["snatch"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex"]},
"sneaker":{"w":"sneaker","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"n. 运动鞋；卑鄙者；鬼鬼祟祟做事的人","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["运动鞋","卑鄙者","鬼鬼祟祟做事的人"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈsniːkə/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈsnikɚ/","usSrc":"Wiktionary"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=sneaker&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"It resembles the kind of small <B>sneaker</B> store you might find in a low-end American mall.","cn":"它类似于你可能在美国低端商场里找到的那种小型运动鞋商店。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"All of them, every <B>sneaker</B>, boot and sandal, every high heel and clog, every flip-flop. What do I do?","cn":"所有的鞋，包括全部的球鞋、靴子、凉鞋，高跟鞋、木屐、人字拖……我该怎么办啊？","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Agile is like the new brand of <B>sneaker</B> that we want to buy to help make our development teams jump higher, run faster.","cn":"敏捷就像一个新品牌的运动鞋，我们买来是想让它帮助我们的开发小组跳得更高，跑得更快。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"The commercial campaign coincides with the release date of the new Nike LeBron 8 <B>sneaker</B>.","cn":"","src":"FORBES","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · FORBES"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"sneak","ph":"/sniːk/","cn":"v. 溜走"},{"w":"sneaky","ph":"/ˈsniːki/","cn":"adj. 鬼鬼祟祟的；暗中的，卑鄙的"},{"w":"sneaking","ph":"/ˈsniːkɪŋ/","cn":"v. 偷偷地走；偷偷地做；偷偷地看；偷拿（不重要"},{"w":"sneakingly","ph":"","cn":"adv. 卑鄙地；偷偷地"}],"syn":[]},"tag":["gk"],"collins":1,"oxford":0,"frq":0,"img":"https://ydlunacommon.nosdn.127.net/d7c019056134ce3393aebd3e6b649d52.png?","syl":{"n":2,"s":0,"l":["snea","ker"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex"]},
