"sunshine":{"w":"sunshine","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"n. 阳光；愉快；晴天；快活","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["阳光","愉快","晴天","快活"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈsʌnʃain/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈsʌnʃaɪn/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=sunshine&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Common sense tells you that you take an umbrella out into a rainstorm, but you leave the umbrella home when you hear a weather forecast for <B>sunshine</B>.","cn":"","src":"2010·天津·阅读D","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2010年高考英语（天津）· 阅读D","year":2010,"region":"天津","section":"阅读D"},{"en":"In winter people come to the Dead Sea to enjoy the <B>sunshine</B>.","cn":"","src":"九年级·阅读理解","srcType":"zhongkao","srcFull":"中考真题 · 阅读理解（该来源未提供年份/地区）","year":0,"section":"阅读理解"},{"en":"So the people there don't get much <B>sunshine</B> in the whole year.","cn":"","src":"七年级·阅读理解","srcType":"zhongkao","srcFull":"中考真题 · 阅读理解（该来源未提供年份/地区）","year":0,"section":"阅读理解"},{"en":"The bay glittered in the <B>sunshine</B>.","cn":"海湾在阳光下闪闪发光。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"sun","ph":"/sʌn/","cn":"n. 太阳；v. 使晒"},{"w":"sunny","ph":"/ˈsʌni/","cn":"adj. 阳光充足的，和煦的；快活的；性情开朗的"},{"w":"sunless","ph":"/ˈsʌnləs/","cn":"adj. 无阳光的，阳光照射不到的，阴暗的"},{"w":"sunnily","ph":"/ˈsʌnɪlɪ/","cn":"adv. 快活地；照着阳光"},{"w":"sunbather","ph":"","cn":"n. 日光浴者；晒太阳的人"},{"w":"sunniness","ph":"/ˈsʌninɪs/","cn":"n. 阳光照射，阳光充足；活泼"}],"syn":["sunlight","sun"]},"tag":["gk","cet4","cet6","ky","toefl"],"collins":2,"oxford":0,"frq":7752,"img":"https://ydlunacommon.nosdn.127.net/8b7908d85a3c2107f4352f7c2df6cc40.png?","syl":{"n":2,"s":0,"l":["sun","shine"]},"flags":[]},
"superb":{"w":"superb","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"adj. 极好的；华丽的；宏伟的；n. (Superb)人名；(罗)苏佩尔布","senses":[{"pos":"adj","cn":["极好的","华丽的","宏伟的"]},{"pos":"n","cn":["(Superb)人名","(罗)苏佩尔布"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/sjuˈpəːb/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/suːˈpɜːrb/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=superb&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Then, one after another, Sydney discovered lots of things that were just sort of there — broad parks, <B>superb</B> beaches, and a culturally diverse population.","cn":"","src":"2022·全国甲卷·阅读D","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2022年高考英语（全国甲卷）· 阅读D","year":2022,"region":"全国甲卷","section":"阅读D"},{"en":"There is a <B>superb</B> 18-hole golf course 6 miles away.","cn":"6英里外有个极好的18洞高尔夫球场。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"It's got a gripping story, great acting, <B>superb</B> sets, and stunning effects.","cn":"电影有扣人心弦的故事情节、精湛的表演、绝妙的布景和惊人的特效。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"He was a Tang poet of <B>superb</B> talent.","cn":"他是一位才华横溢的唐代诗人。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"super","ph":"/ˈsjuːpə/","cn":"adj. 极好的， 上等的； 超级的； 过分的"},{"w":"superbly","ph":"/suːˈpɜːrbli/","cn":"adv. 极好地，出色地，上等地；壮丽地，雄伟地"}],"syn":["brilliant"]},"tag":["gk","cet6","ky","toefl","ielts","gre"],"collins":3,"oxford":0,"frq":6911,"img":"https://0xlei.tech/words/atlas/img/superb.webp","syl":{"n":2,"s":1,"l":["su","perb"]},"flags":["few_exam_ex"]},
