"unmarried":{"w":"unmarried","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"adj. [法] 未婚的；单身的；独身的；v. 离婚（unmarry的过去分词）","senses":[{"pos":"adj","cn":["[法] 未婚的","单身的","独身的"]},{"pos":"v","cn":["离婚（unmarry的过去分词）"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/.ʌnˈmærid/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˌʌnˈmærid/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=unmarried&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Mr is used before the names of men, Mrs is for married women and Miss is for <B>unmarried</B> women.","cn":"","src":"八年级·阅读理解","srcType":"zhongkao","srcFull":"中考真题 · 阅读理解（该来源未提供年份/地区）","year":0,"section":"阅读理解"},{"en":"He is forty two years old, <B>unmarried</B>, and he lives in a big wooden house on Moonlight Road.","cn":"他42岁，未婚，住在月光路上的一所大木屋里。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"After the wedding, the bride will throw her bouquet to the <B>unmarried</B> female guests behind her.","cn":"婚礼结束后，新娘会将她手中的花束抛向身后的未婚女性客人。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Austen is often called the greatest romantic writer, so it is surprising she remained <B>unmarried</B>.","cn":"奥斯汀常被称为最伟大的浪漫作家，所以她一直未婚很令人惊讶。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[],"syn":["single"]},"tag":["gk"],"collins":1,"oxford":0,"frq":9465,"img":"","syl":{"n":3,"s":1,"l":["un","mar","ried"]},"flags":["few_exam_ex","no_img"]},
