"wayside":{"w":"wayside","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"n. 路旁；adj. 路旁的","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["路旁"]},{"pos":"adj","cn":["路旁的"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈweisaid/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈweɪsaɪd/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=wayside&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"We will walk very, very slowly, and if we feel tired we can rest by the <B>wayside</B>.","cn":"我们会走得非常非常慢，如果我们感到累了，我们可以在路边休息。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Research partners Kaitlin Woolley of Cornell University and Ayelet Fishbach of the University of Chicago have made a career out of studying the differences between the goals that people achieve and the ones that fall by the <B>wayside</B>.","cn":"研究搭档康奈尔大学的凯特琳·伍利和芝加哥大学的艾莱特·菲什巴赫以研究人们实现的目标和那些半途而废的目标之间的差异为业。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Amateurs fall by the <B>wayside</B> when the going gets tough.","cn":"初学者们遇到困难就半途而废。","src":"柯林斯","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《柯林斯英汉双解大词典》（有道词典接口）"},{"en":"Often times, they've been, you know, fallen by the <B>wayside</B>, and this time they were funny.","cn":"","src":"NPR","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · NPR"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[],"syn":[]},"tag":["gk"],"collins":0,"oxford":0,"frq":17420,"img":"https://ydlunacommon-cdn.nosdn.127.net/d0fa5bfd6ce073f0a55afd9be643f8e0.jpg?","syl":{"n":2,"s":0,"l":["way","side"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex","fam_gap"]},
