"eastward":{"w":"eastward","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"adv. 向东","senses":[{"pos":"adv","cn":["向东"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈiːstwəd/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈiːstwərd/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=eastward&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"They floated down an <B>eastward</B> flowing river.","cn":"他们顺着一条向东流的河漂流而下。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Saturn still shines in the night though, farther <B>eastward</B> along the ecliptic plane.","cn":"尽管如此，土星仍然在黄道平面向东更远的地方发光。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"The Lapita's thrust into the Pacific was <B>eastward</B>, against the prevailing trade winds, Irwin notes.","cn":"欧文指出，拉皮塔号逆着盛行信风，向东行驶进入太平洋。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"The reduced rebate was negotiated by former Prime Minister Tony Blair to help fund the EU's <B>eastward</B> enlargement.","cn":"","src":"BBC","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · BBC"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"east","ph":"/iːst/","cn":"n. 东方；东风；东方国家；adj. 东方的；向东的；从"},{"w":"eastern","ph":"/ˈiːstən/","cn":"adj. 东方的， 东部的"},{"w":"easterly","ph":"/ˈiːstərli/","cn":"adj. 在东方的；向东的，朝东的；（风）从东方"},{"w":"easternmost","ph":"/ˈiːstərnmoʊst/","cn":"adj. （英）极东的；最东部的（等于 east"},{"w":"eastwards","ph":"/ˈiːstwədz/","cn":"adv. 向东方地；adj. 向东方的"},{"w":"easterner","ph":"/ˈiːstərnər/","cn":"n. 东方人；居住在东部或东方的人"}],"syn":["east"]},"tag":["cet6"],"collins":0,"oxford":0,"frq":14236,"img":"https://0xlei.tech/words/atlas/img/eastward.webp","syl":{"n":2,"s":0,"l":["ea","stward"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex"]},
"injury":{"w":"injury","firstLevel":"高中","cn":"n. 损伤； 受伤处","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["损伤","受伤处"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/ˈindʒəri/","ukSrc":"ECDICT","us":"/ˈɪndʒəri/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=injury&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Indeed, pain is your body telling you something's wrong, and continuing to exercise could lead to serious <B>injury</B>.","cn":"","src":"2014·重庆·阅读B","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2014年高考英语（重庆）· 阅读B","year":2014,"region":"重庆","section":"阅读B"},{"en":"As a result, she says, some of the <B>injuries</B> associated with running, such as runner’s knee, are uncommon among race walkers.","cn":"","src":"2020·新课标Ⅰ卷·阅读C","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2020年高考英语（新课标Ⅰ卷）· 阅读C","year":2020,"region":"新课标Ⅰ卷","section":"阅读C"},{"en":"More than 15% of Jurassic and Cretaceous ichthyosaurs had suffered the bends before they died, but not a single Triassic specimen showed evidence of that sort of <B>injury</B>.","cn":"","src":"2013·江苏·阅读C","srcType":"gaokao","srcFull":"2013年高考英语（江苏）· 阅读C","year":2013,"region":"江苏","section":"阅读C"},{"en":"She's still battling with a knee <B>injury</B>.","cn":"她还在同膝部的伤痛作斗争。","src":"牛津","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"《牛津词典》（有道词典接口）"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"injure","ph":"/ˈindʒə/","cn":"v. 伤害， 损害， 损伤"},{"w":"injured","ph":"/ˈɪndʒərd/","cn":"adj. 受伤的，有伤的；委屈的，受到伤害的；n"},{"w":"injurious","ph":"/ɪnˈdʒʊriəs/","cn":"adj. 有害的，致伤的；中伤的，诽谤的"},{"w":"injuriously","ph":"/ɪnˈdʒʊrɪəsli/","cn":"adv. 有害地；伤害地"}],"syn":["hurt","harm"]},"tag":["gk","cet4","cet6","ky","toefl","ielts"],"collins":4,"oxford":1,"frq":1553,"img":"https://0xlei.tech/words/atlas/img/injury.webp","syl":{"n":3,"s":0,"l":["in","jur","y"]},"flags":[]},
